Landlord’s general obligations for residential premises, Section 52, Residential Tenancies Act 2010', 966, 'https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/rules/landlord-obligations-and-responsibilities-for-rental-properties', 'AU-NSW', '{"license": null, "license_url": null, "rights_status": "pending_review", "rights_url": ["https://www.nsw.gov.au/nsw-government/about-website/copyright"], "usage_status": null}', '{"id": "nsw-landlord-maintenance", "group": "official", "title_zh": "房东维修与维护责任", "title": "Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "english_words": 966, "characters_with_whitespace": 6419, "characters_without_whitespace": 5410, "steps": 0, "source_url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/rules/landlord-obligations-and-responsibilities-for-rental-properties", "text_path": "texts/nsw-landlord-maintenance.txt", "source_metadata": {"document_id": "nsw-landlord-maintenance", "source_id": "nsw-landlord-maintenance", "source_url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/rules/landlord-obligations-and-responsibilities-for-rental-properties", "final_url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/rules/landlord-obligations-and-responsibilities-for-rental-properties", "publisher": "NSW Government", "document_type": "repair_guidance", "topics": ["repairs", "responsibilities"], "jurisdiction": "AU-NSW", "language": "en", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T09:19:45.258106+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "etag": "W/\"1790585827\"", "last_modified": "Mon, 28 Sep 2026 08:57:07 GMT", "raw_sha256": "f1f67ad88348d3d61ae1ec8f5dd2ce7dae8277a3d5fa13b44e4dff44fc21e9ac", "text_sha256": "e605fa8c66b0ef59a4e35eceeb60be113d99c05d7f2d5dde16cd45b2f9bb9331", "rights_status": "pending_review", "review_status": "pending_review", "provenance_type": "official_publication", "title": "Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "sections": [{"heading": "Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties"], "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Landlords have a responsibility to ensure that the property is fit to live in and meets health and safety laws.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "Landlords are responsible for:", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "providing a property that is fit to live in", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "maintaining the rental property in a reasonable state of repair", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "providing and maintaining locks or other security devices to ensure the property is reasonably secure.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "Landlords who do not comply with these obligations will be in breach of the tenancy agreement.", "links": []}]}, {"heading": "Repairs and maintenance in a rental property", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Repairs and maintenance in a rental property"], "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Landlords are responsible for repairing and maintaining the property so that it is in a reasonable state of repair, considering:", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "the age of the property", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "the amount of rent being paid", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "the prospective life of the property.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "This does not mean that the property must be in perfect condition.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "To learn more about landlord obligations for repairs and maintenance, visit Getting repairs done on a rental property .", "links": [{"text": "Getting repairs done on a rental property", "url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/renting-a-place-to-live/getting-repairs-done"}]}]}, {"heading": "Landlords should deal with urgent repairs", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Situations where landlords are required to make repairs to a rental property", "Landlords should deal with urgent repairs"], "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Urgent repairs are considered to be repairs needed for serious issues that make a property unsafe or insecure or prevent access to essential services. That is, an issue that:", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "threatens a property''s structural integrity.", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "poses a risk to lives.", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "makes a property unsafe or insecure.", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "prevents access to essential services.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "Visit the Urgent repairs in residential rental properties page to see a list of what is considered an urgent repair.", "links": [{"text": "Urgent repairs in residential rental properties", "url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/rules/urgent-repairs-residential-rental-properties"}]}]}, {"heading": "Landlords have certain responsibilities after a natural disaster", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Situations where landlords are required to make repairs to a rental property", "Landlords have certain responsibilities after a natural disaster"], "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph", "text": "If a property has been affected by a natural disaster, such as a flood, bushfire or storm, landlords have certain responsibilities.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "Serious storm, fire or flood damage are all considered to be urgent repairs and should be handled quickly.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "Learn more about obligations for landlords after a rental property is affected by a natural disaster .", "links": [{"text": "Learn more about obligations for landlords after a rental property is affected by a natural disaster", "url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/rules/rental-property-affected-by-a-natural-disaster"}]}]}, {"heading": "Summary of key obligations for landlords", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Repairing and maintaining smoke alarms", "Summary of key obligations for landlords"], "blocks": [{"type": "list_item", "text": "Landlords should repair a smoke alarm within certain time frames.", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "Landlords should conduct checks to ensure the smoke alarm is working.", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "Landlords should install or replace removable batteries every year.", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "If the rental property is in a strata scheme, the owners corporation may be responsible for repair and replacement of smoke alarms. Even if that is the case, landlords still have some obligations. See ''Smoke alarms in strata schemes'' below.", "links": []}]}, {"heading": "When are smoke alarms considered not working", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Repairing and maintaining smoke alarms", "Summary of key obligations for landlords", "When are smoke alarms considered not working"], "blocks": [{"type": "list_item", "text": "The smoke alarm is removed and not replaced with a working smoke alarm.", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "The smoke alarm does not work (for example because the battery needs to be replaced).", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "The smoke alarm is malfunctioning (for example due to accumulated dust, insects, airborne contaminants or corrosion of electrical circuitry).", "links": []}]}, {"heading": "Smoke alarms in strata schemes", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Repairing and maintaining smoke alarms", "Summary of key obligations for landlords", "Smoke alarms in strata schemes"], "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Landlords with properties in a strata scheme have an obligation to ensure smoke alarms installed in the property are working. If the owners corporation is responsible for the repair and replacement of smoke alarms, landlords may have some different obligations relating to smoke alarms.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "Visit the Smoke alarms in a rental property page to learn more about landlord obligations and smoke alarms, including in strata schemes.", "links": [{"text": "Smoke alarms in a rental property", "url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/rules/smoke-alarms-a-rental-property"}]}]}, {"heading": "Non-urgent repairs", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Repairing and maintaining smoke alarms", "Non-urgent repairs"], "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph", "text": "A landlord or agent is responsible for arranging non-urgent repairs needed to comply with the landlord''s obligation to maintain a rental property in a reasonable state of repair.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "A tenant must have written permission ''to carry out repairs to a rental property, including agreement on any reimbursement for costs, from the landlord, except for urgent repairs and some smoke alarm repairs, but tenants need to follow the requirements for those repairs.", "links": []}]}, {"heading": "Meeting health and safety laws for a rental property", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Meeting health and safety laws for a rental property"], "blocks": [{"type": "list_item", "text": "Landlords have a responsibility to ensure the property meets health and safety laws.", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "Meeting health and safety laws is a term of every tenancy agreement, and landlords who do not comply with these obligations will be in breach of the agreement.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "Learn more about health and safety in a rental home .", "links": [{"text": "Learn more about health and safety in a rental home", "url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/safety-home"}]}]}, {"heading": "Resolving a repair, maintenance or damage dispute with a tenant", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Resolving a repair, maintenance or damage dispute with a tenant"], "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph", "text": "It is always best for landlords or an agent to try and seek a resolution with a tenant . If an issue cannot be resolved, a landlord can:", "links": [{"text": "seek a resolution with a tenant", "url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/renting-a-place-to-live/resolving-residential-tenancy-disputes"}]}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "contact Fair Trading’s tenancy complaints and disputes service", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "lodge an application directly with the NSW Civil and Administrative Tribunal (NCAT).", "links": [{"text": "NSW Civil and Administrative Tribunal", "url": "https://www.ncat.nsw.gov.au/"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "In some situations, Fair Trading may issue a rectification order to landlords to undertake repairs, or to tenants to fix damage.", "links": []}]}, {"heading": "Get help from NSW Fair Trading", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Resolving a repair, maintenance or damage dispute with a tenant", "Get help from NSW Fair Trading"], "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph", "text": "Ask a question, get support, make a complaint, give feedback or get help with a dispute on matters relating to residential tenancies.", "links": []}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "NSW Fair Trading call centre: 13 32 20", "links": [{"text": "13 32 20", "url": "tel:133220"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "text": "Monday to Friday, 8:30am-5pm", "links": []}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "Make a tenancy or other real estate related enquiry at NSW Fair Trading", "links": [{"text": "Make a tenancy or other real estate related enquiry at NSW Fair Trading", "url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/departments-and-agencies/fair-trading/complaints-and-enquiries"}]}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "Provide feedback or make a complaint to NSW Fair Trading", "links": [{"text": "Provide feedback or make a complaint to NSW Fair Trading", "url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/renting-a-place-to-live/residential-tenancy-complaints"}]}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "Get information and advice about dealing with tenancy disputes", "links": [{"text": "Get information and advice about dealing with tenancy disputes", "url": "https://www.nsw.gov.au/housing-and-construction/renting-a-place-to-live/resolving-residential-tenancy-disputes"}]}]}, {"heading": "Legislation supporting this page", "heading_path": ["Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties", "Legislation supporting this page"], "blocks": [{"type": "list_item", "text": "Security and safety of residential premises, Part 3 Division 7 Residential Tenancies Act 2010", "links": [{"text": "Security and safety of residential premises, Part 3 Division 7 Residential Tenancies Act 2010", "url": "https://legislation.nsw.gov.au/view/html/inforce/2023-08-03/act-2010-042#pt.3-div.7"}]}, {"type": "list_item", "text": "Landlord’s general obligations for residential premises, Section 52, Residential Tenancies Act 2010", "links": [{"text": "Landlord’s general obligations for residential premises, Section 52, Residential Tenancies Act 2010", "url": "https://legislation.nsw.gov.au/view/html/inforce/current/act-2010-042#sec.52"}]}]}], "content_text": "Landlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties\nLandlords have a responsibility to ensure that the property is fit to live in and meets health and safety laws.\nLandlords are responsible for:\nproviding a property that is fit to live in\nmaintaining the rental property in a reasonable state of repair\nproviding and maintaining locks or other security devices to ensure the property is reasonably secure.\nLandlords who do not comply with these obligations will be in breach of the tenancy agreement.\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Repairs and maintenance in a rental property\nLandlords are responsible for repairing and maintaining the property so that it is in a reasonable state of repair, considering:\nthe age of the property\nthe amount of rent being paid\nthe prospective life of the property.\nThis does not mean that the property must be in perfect condition.\nTo learn more about landlord obligations for repairs and maintenance, visit Getting repairs done on a rental property .\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Situations where landlords are required to make repairs to a rental property > Landlords should deal with urgent repairs\nUrgent repairs are considered to be repairs needed for serious issues that make a property unsafe or insecure or prevent access to essential services. That is, an issue that:\nthreatens a property''s structural integrity.\nposes a risk to lives.\nmakes a property unsafe or insecure.\nprevents access to essential services.\nVisit the Urgent repairs in residential rental properties page to see a list of what is considered an urgent repair.\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Situations where landlords are required to make repairs to a rental property > Landlords have certain responsibilities after a natural disaster\nIf a property has been affected by a natural disaster, such as a flood, bushfire or storm, landlords have certain responsibilities.\nSerious storm, fire or flood damage are all considered to be urgent repairs and should be handled quickly.\nLearn more about obligations for landlords after a rental property is affected by a natural disaster .\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Repairing and maintaining smoke alarms > Summary of key obligations for landlords\nLandlords should repair a smoke alarm within certain time frames.\nLandlords should conduct checks to ensure the smoke alarm is working.\nLandlords should install or replace removable batteries every year.\nIf the rental property is in a strata scheme, the owners corporation may be responsible for repair and replacement of smoke alarms. Even if that is the case, landlords still have some obligations. See ''Smoke alarms in strata schemes'' below.\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Repairing and maintaining smoke alarms > Summary of key obligations for landlords > When are smoke alarms considered not working\nThe smoke alarm is removed and not replaced with a working smoke alarm.\nThe smoke alarm does not work (for example because the battery needs to be replaced).\nThe smoke alarm is malfunctioning (for example due to accumulated dust, insects, airborne contaminants or corrosion of electrical circuitry).\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Repairing and maintaining smoke alarms > Summary of key obligations for landlords > Smoke alarms in strata schemes\nLandlords with properties in a strata scheme have an obligation to ensure smoke alarms installed in the property are working. If the owners corporation is responsible for the repair and replacement of smoke alarms, landlords may have some different obligations relating to smoke alarms.\nVisit the Smoke alarms in a rental property page to learn more about landlord obligations and smoke alarms, including in strata schemes.\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Repairing and maintaining smoke alarms > Non-urgent repairs\nA landlord or agent is responsible for arranging non-urgent repairs needed to comply with the landlord''s obligation to maintain a rental property in a reasonable state of repair.\nA tenant must have written permission ''to carry out repairs to a rental property, including agreement on any reimbursement for costs, from the landlord, except for urgent repairs and some smoke alarm repairs, but tenants need to follow the requirements for those repairs.\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Meeting health and safety laws for a rental property\nLandlords have a responsibility to ensure the property meets health and safety laws.\nMeeting health and safety laws is a term of every tenancy agreement, and landlords who do not comply with these obligations will be in breach of the agreement.\nLearn more about health and safety in a rental home .\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Resolving a repair, maintenance or damage dispute with a tenant\nIt is always best for landlords or an agent to try and seek a resolution with a tenant . If an issue cannot be resolved, a landlord can:\ncontact Fair Trading’s tenancy complaints and disputes service\nlodge an application directly with the NSW Civil and Administrative Tribunal (NCAT).\nIn some situations, Fair Trading may issue a rectification order to landlords to undertake repairs, or to tenants to fix damage.\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Resolving a repair, maintenance or damage dispute with a tenant > Get help from NSW Fair Trading\nAsk a question, get support, make a complaint, give feedback or get help with a dispute on matters relating to residential tenancies.\nNSW Fair Trading call centre: 13 32 20\nMonday to Friday, 8:30am-5pm\nMake a tenancy or other real estate related enquiry at NSW Fair Trading\nProvide feedback or make a complaint to NSW Fair Trading\nGet information and advice about dealing with tenancy disputes\n\nLandlord responsibilities for repair and maintenance of rental properties > Legislation supporting this page\nSecurity and safety of residential premises, Part 3 Division 7 Residential Tenancies Act 2010\nLandlord’s general obligations for residential premises, Section 52, Residential Tenancies Act 2010", "rights_url": ["https://www.nsw.gov.au/nsw-government/about-website/copyright"], "extraction_warnings": [], "published_at": "2024-02-01", "source_updated_at": "2026-09-25", "extractor_version": "1.1"}, "text_sha256": "e605fa8c66b0ef59a4e35eceeb60be113d99c05d7f2d5dde16cd45b2f9bb9331"}') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, title_zh=EXCLUDED.title_zh, document_type=EXCLUDED.document_type, body=EXCLUDED.body, english_words=EXCLUDED.english_words, source_url=EXCLUDED.source_url, jurisdiction=EXCLUDED.jurisdiction, license_info=EXCLUDED.license_info, metadata=EXCLUDED.metadata;


Use pliers (or tweezers if the hole is very small) to clean out hole by removing the drywall out of the hole.

Use scissors to cut drywall mesh.

To ensure that the entire hole is covered, cut a piece of mesh larger than the size of the hole.

Use a damp sponge to apply moisture to make the mesh stick to the wall, covering the entire hole.

Use a drywall knife to apply the drywall compound over the mesh. Make sure to spread a generous amount over the entire mesh.

Let the compound dry for about 30 minutes.

You can speed up the drying process by placing a fan directly in front of the drying compound.

Once compound is dry, use sandpaper to smooth out the entire surface of the dried compound.

Paint over the surface with a paint brush.

Use paint that matches the rest of the wall for best results.', 280, 'https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/How+to+Fix+a+Hole+In+Drywall/104072', NULL, '{"license": "CC-BY-NC-SA-3.0", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/", "rights_status": null, "rights_url": null, "usage_status": "project_noncommercial_status_unconfirmed"}', '{"id": "104072", "group": "ifixit", "title_zh": "修补石膏板墙洞", "title": "How to Fix a Hole In Drywall", "english_words": 280, "characters_with_whitespace": 1480, "characters_without_whitespace": 1190, "steps": 6, "source_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/How+to+Fix+a+Hole+In+Drywall/104072", "text_path": "texts/104072.txt", "source_metadata": {"category": "wall_hole", "guide_id": 104072, "api_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/api/2.0/guides/104072", "status": "success", "quality_accepted": false, "knowledge_base_imported": false, "usage_approved": false, "license": "CC-BY-NC-SA-3.0", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/", "usage_status": "project_noncommercial_status_unconfirmed", "record_type": "repair_guide_not_work_order", "source_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/How+to+Fix+a+Hole+In+Drywall/104072", "title": "How to Fix a Hole In Drywall", "author": {"userid": 2356314, "username": "Darrian Johnson", "unique_username": "djohnson17", "join_date": 1517205889, "image": {"id": -32, "guid": "default_avatar_placeholder_guid", "original": "https://assets.cdn.ifixit.com/static/images/avatars/User/ifixit/avatar-12", "mini": "https://assets.cdn.ifixit.com/static/images/avatars/User/ifixit/avatar-12.mini", "thumbnail": "https://assets.cdn.ifixit.com/static/images/avatars/User/ifixit/avatar-12.thumbnail", "140x105": "https://assets.cdn.ifixit.com/static/images/avatars/User/ifixit/avatar-12.140x105", "200x150": "https://assets.cdn.ifixit.com/static/images/avatars/User/ifixit/avatar-12.200x150", "standard": "https://assets.cdn.ifixit.com/static/images/avatars/User/ifixit/avatar-12.standard", "440x330": "https://assets.cdn.ifixit.com/static/images/avatars/User/ifixit/avatar-12.440x330", "medium": "https://assets.cdn.ifixit.com/static/images/avatars/User/ifixit/avatar-12.medium", "large": "https://assets.cdn.ifixit.com/static/images/avatars/User/ifixit/avatar-12.large"}, "reputation": 448, "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/User/2356314/Darrian+Johnson", "teams": [27573]}, "revision_id": 2337959, "source_sha256": "702f4db691d540c230d6abe41daad43a3ecbaad1a528864d896bf4681c466beb", "raw_path": "raw/104072.json", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-05T09:21:23.368170+00:00", "summary": "Have you ever opened a door too hard and it hit...", "introduction": "Have you ever opened a door too hard and it hit the wall causing a small hole in the wall? This is a problem that so many people have, especially with children in the home. Most modern homes have walls made of a material called drywall. A hole in drywall is very easy to patch. It requires no prior skill or experience. This fix requires inexpensive tools and materials that you may find at a local hardware store or you may even already have some of these items at home. This is a guide  on how to patch a small hole in the wall for beginners. This guide will include a complete step by step guide along with all tools and materials that are needed to complete this task.", "difficulty": "Moderate", "tools": [{"type": "", "quantity": 1, "text": "Sand Paper", "notes": null, "url": "http://www.amazon.com/3M-9005NA-Aluminum-Sandpaper-Assorted/dp/B00004Z48U/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1377552439&sr=8-1&keywords=sand+paper", "wiki_url": "/Item/Sand_paper", "wiki_title": "Sand paper", "thumbnail": null, "isoptional": false, "featured": false}, {"type": "", "quantity": 1, "text": "Paint Brush", "notes": null, "url": "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=paint+brushes&crid=13X8SWFKO3UFK&sprefix=paint+brushes%2Caps%2C350&ref=nb_sb_noss_2", "wiki_url": "/Item/Paintbrush", "wiki_title": "Paintbrush", "thumbnail": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/ZGg2LqL6duEdg2ZC.thumbnail", "isoptional": false, "featured": false}, {"type": "", "quantity": 1, "text": "All-Purpose Sponge", "notes": null, "url": "http://www.amazon.com/QEP-70005-36-XL-All-purpose-sponge/dp/B001B0GQHO/ref=sr_1_4?ie=UTF8&qid=1443047297&sr=8-4&keywords=large+sponge", "wiki_url": "/Item/Porous_Car_Washing_Sponge", "wiki_title": "Porous Car Washing Sponge", "thumbnail": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/uHDPfJkrj44BQLVA.thumbnail", "isoptional": false, "featured": false}, {"type": "", "quantity": 1, "text": "Scissors", "notes": null, "url": "/Item/Scissors", "wiki_url": "/Item/Scissors", "wiki_title": "Scissors", "thumbnail": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/kDqaHmByxsoEUAuR.thumbnail", "isoptional": false, "featured": false}, {"type": "", "quantity": 1, "text": "Small Chain Nose Pliers", "notes": null, "url": "https://www.amazon.com/Jewelry-Pliers-Shynek-Wrapping-Supplies/dp/B07ZGFK411/ref=sr_1_3?crid=MGXSMIOVU34G&keywords=Small+Chain+Nose+Pliers&qid=1672157790&sprefix=small+chain+nose+pliers%2Caps%2C64&sr=8-3", "wiki_url": "/Item/Small_Chain_Nose_Pliers", "wiki_title": "Small Chain Nose Pliers", "thumbnail": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/rsaulVrA2eRC4TZn.thumbnail", "isoptional": false, "featured": false}, {"type": "", "quantity": 1, "text": "Tweezers", "notes": null, "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/en-au/products/tweezers?variant=53717116387696", "wiki_url": "/Item/Tweezers", "wiki_title": "Tweezers", "thumbnail": "https://cart-products.cdn.ifixit.com/cart-products/dHWMTxibZKNbXnxu.thumbnail", "isoptional": false, "featured": false}, {"type": "", "quantity": 1, "text": "Putty Knife", "notes": null, "url": "https://www.amazon.com/HAUTMEC-3pc-Putty-Knife-1-25/dp/B07GYCCLCJ/", "wiki_url": "/Item/Putty_knife", "wiki_title": "Putty knife", "thumbnail": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/HweGvS4NQHSqBFeX.thumbnail", "isoptional": false, "featured": false}], "steps": [{"step_id": 195001, "order": 1, "title": "", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Use pliers (or [product|IF145-020|tweezers] if the hole is very small) to clean out hole by removing the drywall out of the hole.", "bullet": "red", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Use pliers (or <a href=\"https://www.ifixit.com/en-au/products/tweezers\" class=\"product-link\">tweezers</a> if the hole is very small) to clean out hole by removing the drywall out of the hole."}]}, {"step_id": 195003, "order": 2, "title": "", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Use scissors to cut drywall mesh.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Use scissors to cut drywall mesh."}, {"text_raw": "To ensure that the entire hole is covered, cut a piece of mesh larger than the size of the hole.", "bullet": "icon_note", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "To ensure that the entire hole is covered, cut a piece of mesh larger than the size of the hole."}]}, {"step_id": 195746, "order": 3, "title": "", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Use a damp sponge to apply moisture to make the mesh stick to the wall, covering the entire hole.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Use a damp sponge to apply moisture to make the mesh stick to the wall, covering the entire hole."}]}, {"step_id": 195004, "order": 4, "title": "", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Use a drywall knife to apply the drywall compound over the mesh. Make sure to spread a generous amount over the entire mesh.", "bullet": "red", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Use a drywall knife to apply the drywall compound over the mesh. Make sure to spread a generous amount over the entire mesh."}, {"text_raw": "Let the compound dry for about 30 minutes.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Let the compound dry for about 30 minutes."}, {"text_raw": "You can speed up the drying process by placing a fan directly in front of the drying compound.", "bullet": "icon_note", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "You can speed up the drying process by placing a fan directly in front of the drying compound."}]}, {"step_id": 195005, "order": 5, "title": "", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Once compound is dry, use sandpaper to smooth out the entire surface of the dried compound.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Once compound is dry, use sandpaper to smooth out the entire surface of the dried compound."}]}, {"step_id": 195006, "order": 6, "title": "", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Paint over the surface with a paint brush.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Paint over the surface with a paint brush."}, {"text_raw": "Use paint that matches the rest of the wall for best results.", "bullet": "icon_note", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Use paint that matches the rest of the wall for best results."}]}], "safety_review": "pending_model_and_Australian_context_review"}, "text_sha256": "b7006c675f25d25ac61c16f9a12aa881dc916074b1ab2861cff55ef297a7219d"}') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, title_zh=EXCLUDED.title_zh, document_type=EXCLUDED.document_type, body=EXCLUDED.body, english_words=EXCLUDED.english_words, source_url=EXCLUDED.source_url, jurisdiction=EXCLUDED.jurisdiction, license_info=EXCLUDED.license_info, metadata=EXCLUDED.metadata;


