The number and head type/length of the screws may vary from faucet to faucet.', '{"step_id": 88089, "order": 4, "title": "", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Use a screwdriver to remove the single handle screw.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Use a screwdriver to remove the single handle screw."}, {"text_raw": "The number and head type/length of the screws may vary from faucet to faucet.", "bullet": "icon_note", "level": 1, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "The number and head type/length of the screws may vary from faucet to faucet."}]}') ON CONFLICT (document_id, step_number) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, body=EXCLUDED.body, metadata=EXCLUDED.metadata;


When removing the temperature limit stop and indexer, take note of their position. The limit stop and indexer determine the maximum temperature that water can reach when coming out of the faucet.
Even if you mark the position of the indexer and stop, you may still need to reset the temperature limit after addressing the leak. Follow the instructions for your specific faucet if they are available.', '{"step_id": 88091, "order": 6, "title": "", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Remove the temperature limit stop from the top of the cartridge.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Remove the temperature limit stop from the top of the cartridge."}, {"text_raw": "When removing the temperature limit stop and indexer, take note of their position. The limit stop and indexer determine the maximum temperature that water can reach when coming out of the faucet.", "bullet": "icon_note", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "When removing the temperature limit stop and indexer, take note of their position. The limit stop and indexer determine the maximum temperature that water can reach when coming out of the faucet."}, {"text_raw": "Even if you mark the position of the indexer and stop, you ''''may'''' still need to [http://www.us.kohler.com/webassets/kpna/catalog/pdf/en/1202228_2.pdf|reset the temperature limit|new_window=true] after addressing the leak. Follow the instructions for your specific faucet if they are available.", "bullet": "icon_reminder", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Even if you mark the position of the indexer and stop, you <em>may</em> still need to <a href=\"http://www.us.kohler.com/webassets/kpna/catalog/pdf/en/1202228_2.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">reset the temperature limit</a> after addressing the leak. Follow the instructions for your specific faucet if they are available."}]}') ON CONFLICT (document_id, step_number) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, body=EXCLUDED.body, metadata=EXCLUDED.metadata;






If the leak has been coming only from the end of the faucet, replace the cartridge.
If the faucet has been leaking from the base or from the faucet handle, replace the o-rings.
When installing new o-rings, be sure to properly seat them into the grooves on the underside of the cartridge. A misaligned o-ring can easily cause a new leak.', '{"step_id": 88097, "order": 12, "title": "", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Remove the cartridge o-rings.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Remove the cartridge o-rings."}, {"text_raw": "If the leak has been coming only from the end of the faucet, replace the cartridge.", "bullet": "icon_note", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "If the leak has been coming only from the end of the faucet, replace the cartridge."}, {"text_raw": "If the faucet has been leaking from the base or from the faucet handle, replace the o-rings.", "bullet": "icon_note", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "If the faucet has been leaking from the base or from the faucet handle, replace the o-rings."}, {"text_raw": "When installing new o-rings, be sure to properly seat them into the grooves on the underside of the cartridge. A misaligned o-ring can easily cause a new leak.", "bullet": "icon_reminder", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "When installing new o-rings, be sure to properly seat them into the grooves on the underside of the cartridge. A misaligned o-ring can easily cause a new leak."}]}') ON CONFLICT (document_id, step_number) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, body=EXCLUDED.body, metadata=EXCLUDED.metadata;



Before starting, make sure your sink is empty.

Clear out the sink using a cup or sponge to remove any standing water for better suction.

If your stopper is attached to the p-trap, removing it may cause water to leak. Be ready to duct tape it or have a towel or small bucket to catch the leak.

If your sink has a stopper plug, take it out.

This will give direct access to the clogged drain and improve suction.

Most sinks have detached stopper plugs. However, some sink stoppers are connected to the p-trap, so check which type you have and adjust accordingly.

If your sink has an overflow hole, cover it with duct tape or a towel to seal it.

This helps maintain suction and prevents water from leaking through it.

Ensure that your vacuum can suck up water, using a regular vacuum could cause damage to the vacuum.

Before setting up, open your wet vacuum so it’s ready for use.

Check the settings on your vacuum to see if your filter is good for wet or dry use.

Remove the filter to avoid potential damage.

As a precaution, it''s recommended to remove the filter even if it''s designed for wet use to prevent potential damage over time.

Position the vacuum hose directly over the drain.

Press the hose firmly against the drain.

If needed, add an inch of water to the sink before attaching the hose, this can help improve suction.

Switch the vacuum to wet mode and turn it on.

Hold the hose over the drain for about two minutes to pull up the clog.

The vacuum tank may fill up quickly, so be prepared to empty it once or twice during the process.

Check the vacuum hose for debris every few minutes.

If hair or gunk comes up, remove it by hand or with needle-nose pliers before continuing.

Remove the hose from the sink.

Run water to see if the clog is cleared. If water still drains slowly, repeat the process or consider seeking professional assistance.', 469, 'https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/How+to+Unclog+a+Sink+Using+a+Wet+Vacuum/182837', NULL, '{"license": "CC-BY-NC-SA-3.0", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/", "rights_status": null, "rights_url": null, "usage_status": "project_noncommercial_status_unconfirmed"}', '{"id": "182837", "group": "ifixit", "title_zh": "用湿式吸尘器疏通水槽", "title": "How to Unclog a Sink Using a Wet Vacuum", "english_words": 469, "characters_with_whitespace": 2621, "characters_without_whitespace": 2131, "steps": 9, "source_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/How+to+Unclog+a+Sink+Using+a+Wet+Vacuum/182837", "text_path": "texts/182837.txt", "source_metadata": {"category": "sink_blockage", "guide_id": 182837, "api_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/api/2.0/guides/182837", "status": "success", "quality_accepted": false, "knowledge_base_imported": false, "usage_approved": false, "license": "CC-BY-NC-SA-3.0", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/", "usage_status": "project_noncommercial_status_unconfirmed", "record_type": "repair_guide_not_work_order", "source_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/How+to+Unclog+a+Sink+Using+a+Wet+Vacuum/182837", "title": "How to Unclog a Sink Using a Wet Vacuum", "author": {"userid": 4637178, "username": "Monica Collazo-Cofino", "unique_username": "monicacollazo", "join_date": 1736700172, "image": {"id": 3528143, "guid": "OoMBlomiOij45xMI", "mini": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/OoMBlomiOij45xMI.mini", "thumbnail": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/OoMBlomiOij45xMI.thumbnail", "140x105": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/OoMBlomiOij45xMI.140x105", "200x150": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/OoMBlomiOij45xMI.200x150", "standard": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/OoMBlomiOij45xMI.standard", "original": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/OoM