_blade_screwdriver", "wiki_url": "/Item/Plastic_Opening_Tools_flat_blade_screwdriver", "wiki_title": "Plastic Opening Tools flat blade screwdriver", "thumbnail": null, "isoptional": false, "featured": false}, {"type": "", "quantity": 1, "text": "Channellock Groove Joint Pliers", "notes": null, "url": "http://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_noss?url=search-alias%3Daps&field-keywords=Channellock%20Groove%20Joint%20Pliers", "wiki_url": "/Item/Channellock_Groove_Joint_Pliers", "wiki_title": "Channellock Groove Joint Pliers", "thumbnail": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/weV1bSwAMJCQgeSU.thumbnail", "isoptional": false, "featured": false}, {"type": "", "quantity": 2, "text": "Shop Towel", "notes": null, "url": "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=shop+towels+reusable&crid=TAT2IDQHOVU6&sprefix=shop+towels%2Caps%2C345&ref=nb_sb_ss_saint-en-refocus-candidate_9_11", "wiki_url": "/Item/Towel", "wiki_title": "Towel", "thumbnail": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/iiyVFeyBM14s4YMC.thumbnail", "isoptional": false, "featured": false}, {"type": "", "quantity": 1, "text": "Large Bowl", "notes": null, "url": "https://www.amazon.com/Pyrex-Prepware-4-Quart-Rimmed-Mixing/dp/B07473FZXQ/ref=sr_1_40?keywords=large+bowl&qid=1653409089&sr=8-40", "wiki_url": "/Item/Bowl", "wiki_title": "Bowl", "thumbnail": null, "isoptional": false, "featured": false}], "steps": [{"step_id": 198987, "order": 1, "title": "Safety precautions", "lines": [{"text_raw": "''''''UNPLUG POWER CORD; TURN OFF WATER SUPPLY.''''''", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "<strong>UNPLUG POWER CORD; TURN OFF WATER SUPPLY.</strong>"}, {"text_raw": "Check machine details on the inside of the main door.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Check machine details on the inside of the main door."}]}, {"step_id": 198988, "order": 2, "title": "Remove top cover", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Move washing machine away from wall to make rear and front accessible.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Move washing machine away from wall to make rear and front accessible."}, {"text_raw": "Using Torx T20, unscrew two screws (top left and top right on rear side) .", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Using Torx T20, unscrew two screws (top left and top right on rear side) ."}, {"text_raw": "Slide top backwards, lift it off, and put it aside.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Slide top backwards, lift it off, and put it aside."}]}, {"step_id": 198991, "order": 3, "title": "Remove detergent dispensing tray, and 3 screws", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Push down blue part in the middle to release the tray, and pull it out completely.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Push down blue part in the middle to release the tray, and pull it out completely."}, {"text_raw": "Unscrew three T20 screws; the one on the lower right is shorter.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Unscrew three T20 screws; the one on the lower right is shorter."}]}, {"step_id": 198995, "order": 4, "title": "Remove control panel", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Unhook three hooks at the top (two shown).", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Unhook three hooks at the top (two shown)."}, {"text_raw": "On the inside, on the right, there is another hook (marked), sitting between two guiding notches without hooks.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "On the inside, on the right, there is another hook (marked), sitting between two guiding notches without hooks."}]}, {"step_id": 198996, "order": 5, "title": "Disconnect control panel", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Release the cables by gently pressing the hooked guides. Note that the black part (marked by a rectangle) must be unlocked.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Release the cables by gently pressing the hooked guides. Note that the black part (marked by a rectangle) must be unlocked."}, {"text_raw": "Finally, unlock the connector (e.g. with your nails or a flat-blade screwdriver) and pull it out.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Finally, unlock the connector (e.g. with your nails or a flat-blade screwdriver) and pull it out."}, {"text_raw": "Put the control panel aside.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Put the control panel aside."}]}, {"step_id": 198997, "order": 6, "title": "Immobilize the tumbler unit", "lines": [{"text_raw": "The drum is freely suspended. Wedge a towel on the rear side behind the drum to immobilize it. This will prevent damage when tilting the washing machine later on.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "The drum is freely suspended. Wedge a towel on the rear side behind the drum to immobilize it. This will prevent damage when tilting the washing machine later on."}, {"text_raw": "***DO NOT FORGET TO REMOVE THIS when reassembling!***", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "<strong>DO NOT FORGET TO REMOVE THIS when reassembling!</strong>"}]}, {"step_id": 198999, "order": 7, "title": "Detach door seal from front cover", "lines": [{"text_raw": "The rubber door seal is attached to the front cover by a metal wire and a spring.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "The rubber door seal is attached to the front cover by a metal wire and a spring."}, {"text_raw": "Pry out the spring and pull away the wire.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Pry out the spring and pull away the wire."}, {"text_raw": "Unpeel the seal all the way round, and tuck it inside.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Unpeel the seal all the way round, and tuck it inside."}]}, {"step_id": 199010, "order": 8, "title": "Remove drain/filter door, drain water, and unscrew", "lines": [{"text_raw": "The round door (front bottom right) for the drain tube and filter can be removed, by opening it completely, and gently pulling out the left side of the hinge.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "The round door (front bottom right) for the drain tube and filter can be removed, by opening it completely, and gently pulling out the left side of the hinge."}, {"text_raw": "''''''DRAIN ANY REMAINING WATER''''''.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "<strong>DRAIN ANY REMAINING WATER</strong>."}, {"text_raw": "Unscrew two T20 screws.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Unscrew two T20 screws."}]}, {"step_id": 199014, "order": 9, "title": "Unscrew front cover", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Unscrew two (T20) screws at the top.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Unscrew two (T20) screws at the top."}, {"text_raw": "Tilt the whole washing machine towards its rear side to expose the front bottom. Lean it against a wall.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Tilt the whole washing machine towards its rear side to expose the front bottom. Lean it against a wall."}, {"text_raw": "Unscrew two (6mm hex-head) screws on the bottom.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Unscrew two (6mm hex-head) screws on the bottom."}]}, {"step_id": 199017, "order": 10, "title": "Remove front cover", "lines": [{"text_raw": "The front cover is held in place by plastic hooked pins. Slightly lift the front cover to unhook it.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "The front cover is held in place by plastic hooked pins. Slightly lift the front cover to unhook it."}, {"text_raw": "On the inside, unclip something, and pull out a connector (for the door lock). The plastic emergency door release comes out easily. The image shows this when clip and connector are already disconnected.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "On the inside, unclip something, and pull out a connector (for the door lock). The plastic emergency door release comes out easily. The image shows this when clip and connector are already disconnected."}, {"text_raw": "''''''DO NOT FORGET TO PUT ALL THIS BACK on reassembly!''''''", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "<strong>DO NOT FORGET TO PUT ALL THIS BACK on reassembly!</strong>"}]}, {"step_id": 199018, "order": 11, "title": "Remove plastic strip", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Remove the plastic strip that protects the bottom edge.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Remove the plastic strip that protects the bottom edge."}, {"text_raw": "Unhook on the back, and tilt it forwards.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Unhook on the back, and tilt it forwards."}, {"text_raw": "Note the guiding notches to help you put it back.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Note the guiding notches to help you put it back."}]}, {"step_id": 199020, "order": 12, "title": "Remove drain/filter cover plate", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Unscrew one (T20) screw.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Unscrew one (T20) screw."}, {"text_raw": "Tilt the plate back, and lift it. There is a hooked tab, and a guiding pin to help you reassemble the plate.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Tilt the plate back, and lift it. There is a hooked tab, and a guiding pin to help you reassemble the plate."}, {"text_raw": "Pull out the drain tube.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Pull out the drain tube."}, {"text_raw": "Put the cover plate aside.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Put the cover plate aside."}]}, {"step_id": 199025, "order": 13, "title": "Disconnect pump", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Pull the power connector from the pump.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Pull the power connector from the pump."}, {"text_raw": "Using pliers, loosen the clamp on the hose from the tumbler and slide it back.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Using pliers, loosen the clamp on the hose from the tumbler and slide it back."}, {"text_raw": "Remove the hose.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Remove the hose."}, {"text_raw": "BE PREPARED FOR SOME WATER (use a towel or bowl).", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "BE PREPARED FOR SOME WATER (use a towel or bowl)."}]}, {"step_id": 199026, "order": 14, "title": "Remove debris", "lines": [{"text_raw": "In my case, the pump inlet (where we just removed the hose coming from the tumbler) was clogged with debris and some cloth.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "In my case, the pump inlet (where we just removed the hose coming from the tumbler) was clogged with debris and some cloth."}, {"text_raw": "This prevented draining, and even prevented removal of the filter. Thus, requiring disassembly. But we are not done yet.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "This prevented draining, and even prevented removal of the filter. Thus, requiring disassembly. But we are not done yet."}]}, {"step_id": 199027, "order": 15, "title": "Detach filter/pump unit", "lines": [{"text_raw": "Unscrew four T20 screws.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Unscrew four T20 screws."}, {"text_raw": "Tilt the filter/pump unit (note the tab at the top), and pull it out from the back.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "Tilt the filter/pump unit (note the tab at the top), and pull it out from the back."}]}, {"step_id": 199028, "order": 16, "title": "Clean inlet, filter, and pump", "lines": [{"text_raw": "At his point you can clean the water inlet, the filter, and the pump. The impeller should move freely. The pump itself can also be removed to replace it (but I did not do that).", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "At his point you can clean the water inlet, the filter, and the pump. The impeller should move freely. The pump itself can also be removed to replace it (but I did not do that)."}, {"text_raw": "In my case, a significant amount of cloth got stuck in the water inlet, including a necklace. In the filter, there were some hairpins, and inside the pump itself, a coin and a pendent. LESSON: CLEAN THE FILTER MORE OFTEN, while you can stil remove it without disassembling the machine.", "bullet": "black", "level": 0, "lineid": null, "text_rendered": "In my case, a significant amount of cloth got stuck in the water inlet, including a necklace. In the filter, there were some hairpins, and inside the pump itself, a coin and a pendent. LESSON: CLEAN THE FILTER MORE OFTEN, while you can stil remove it without disassembling the machine."}]}], "safety_review": "pending_model_and_Australian_context_review"}, "text_sha256": "b3c7dd9b7adb2535430121ea33782ac43a43f9a72266253f282f1c442051fcaa"}') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, title_zh=EXCLUDED.title_zh, document_type=EXCLUDED.document_type, body=EXCLUDED.body, english_words=EXCLUDED.english_words, source_url=EXCLUDED.source_url, jurisdiction=EXCLUDED.jurisdiction, license_info=EXCLUDED.license_info, metadata=EXCLUDED.metadata;

