mpt-to-fix-a-sink-leak-myself", "role": "reported_fault_context_candidate", "status": "success", "rights_status": "unknown", "width": 1512, "height": 2016, "final_url": "https://i.sstatic.net/WjYMS.jpg", "local_path": "media/000/05.jpg", "sha256": "748cf4ce765f5010e719ffea725414f9e1ae60aa6160ee7ef4b18707fe0748c8", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-09T08:52:10.241206+00:00"}}, {"file": "repair-integrated-20261009\\dataset.json", "record": {"id": "indoor-162279-0", "group": "indoor", "category": "pipe_leak", "category_zh": "管道漏水", "title": "Should I attempt to fix a sink leak myself?", "reported_symptom": "I have a slow leak under my kitchen sink, in what I think is the top-most screw thread in the photo below. It leaks when the sink is full. EDIT: specifically, I think the leak is between the gray sink pipe and the off-white pipe right at the top. I am very practical (carpentry and such) but have zero plumbing experience. Even with sinks. Can I \"just\" buy some parts and connect them up? Like water lego Thanks!", "display_label": "管道漏水", "label_basis": "reported_symptom_context", "demo_status": "待维修（演示设定）", "demo_status_is_synthetic": true, "actual_work_order": false, "diagnosis_confirmed": false, "source_url": "https://diy.stackexchange.com/questions/162279/should-i-attempt-to-fix-a-sink-leak-myself", "image_url": "https://i.sstatic.net/WjYMS.jpg", "author": "mafrosis", "content_license": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/", "image_rights_status": "not_independently_verified", "source_record_file": "D:\\project\\Safescan_agent\\data\\collection-pilot\\indoor-repair-20261009\\clean.json", "source_image_path": "D:\\project\\Safescan_agent\\data\\collection-pilot\\indoor-repair-20261009\\media\\000\\05.jpg", "review_note": "管道及接头照片与漏水帖子对应；不保证每张可见滴水。", "local_path": "images/indoor-162279-0.jpg", "sha256": "748cf4ce765f5010e719ffea725414f9e1ae60aa6160ee7ef4b18707fe0748c8", "country": null}}, {"file": "indoor-repair-20261009\\media\\00