achine-drain-leak-back-up", "role": "reported_fault_context_candidate", "status": "success", "rights_status": "unknown", "width": 1600, "height": 2844, "final_url": "https://i.sstatic.net/9n5qf.jpg", "local_path": "media/020/10.jpg", "sha256": "9dd59c7a690333f934aa40f1d29d64397ba52fd02b8a845b683f7d45b5ef0382", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-09T08:53:05.001481+00:00"}}, {"file": "repair-integrated-20261009\\dataset.json", "record": {"id": "indoor-211998-0", "group": "indoor", "category": "appliance_leak", "category_zh": "家电漏水", "title": "Washing machine drain leak / back up", "reported_symptom": "Hi I recently bought a new Beko washing machine with dryer (model WD75141), just after 5-6 washes I saw water leakage on the floor, most probably drain water by the looks of it. I am no expert my question is does this water also back flow into the laundry and subsequently the laundry is still dirty? The drain pipe goes to a drain hose around 90cm high the same height as the washing machine and in the instructions it says maximum 90cm. I saw the water leakage mid cycle, and afterwards I saw the washing machine removing water and filling drum with new water and spinning because in this cycle I did not see detergent bubbles in water. My question if the washing machine does that does it mean laundry is dirty? I am not sure if there could be a backup of water. Since the machine is a washer-dryer, at the end clothes were less dry than usual because the clothes got wrapped into a bed sheet which perhaps prevented drying, I am not sure. This drying less happened to me once before with another washing machine because of the same bed sheet.", "display_label": "家电漏水", "label_basis": "reported_symptom_context", "demo_status": "待维修（演示设定）", "demo_status_is_synthetic": true, "actual_work_order": false, "diagnosis_confirmed": false, "source_url": "https://diy.stackexchange.com/questions/211998/washing-machine-drain-leak-back-up", "image_url": "https://i.sstatic.net/9n5qf.jpg", "author": "a.m.2456", "content_license": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/", "image_rights_status": "not_independently_verified", "source_record_file": "D:\\project\\Safescan_agent\\data\\collection-pilot\\indoor-repair-20261009\\clean.json", "source_image_path": "D:\\project\\Safescan_agent\\data\\collection-pilot\\indoor-repair-20261009\\media\\020\\10.jpg", "review_note": "洗衣机、软管连接或阀门照片；不能一律标成机器本体损坏。", "local_path": "images/indoor-211998-0.jpg", "sha256": "9dd59c7a690333f934aa40f1d29d64397ba52fd02b8a845b683f7d45b5ef0382", "country": null}}, {"file": "indoor-repair-20261009\\media\\020\\outcomes.json", "record": {"id": "211998-0", "question_id": 211998, "category": "appliance_leak", "kind": "image", "url": "https://i.sstatic.net/9n5qf.jpg", "alt": "enter image description here", "source_url": "https://diy.stackexchange.com/questions/211998/washing-machine-drain-leak-back-up", "role": "reported_fault_context_candidate", "status": "success", "rights_status": "unknown", "width": 1600, "height": 2844, "final_url": "https://i.sstatic.net/9n5qf.jpg", "local_path": "10.jpg", "sha256": "9dd59c7a690333f934aa40f1d29d64397ba52fd02b8a845b683f7d45b5ef0382", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-09T08:53:05.001481+00:00"}}]}') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET bucket=EXCLUDED.bucket, object_key=EXCLUDED.object_key, mime_type=EXCLUDED.mime_type, byte_size=EXCLUDED.byte_size, width=EXCLUDED.width, height=EXCLUDED.height, source_url=EXCLUDED.source_url, metadata=EXCLUDED.metadata;
